  "tagline": "Fast SQL-first search database, forked from Sphinx, with columnar storage and vector KNN.",
  "description": "Manticore Search forked from Sphinx 2.3 in 2017 and has since become a full search database: real-time tables, a MySQL-protocol SQL interface, an Elasticsearch-like JSON API, columnar storage, joins and HNSW vector search. It is noticeably lighter on resources than Elasticsearch and often faster for full-text and log-style queries on a single box. Replication is Galera-based and distribution across nodes is done with distributed tables. A good fit if you like SQL, want an open-source (GPL-3.0) engine, and do not need the Elastic ecosystem.",
